// retroverse-cli worldplan generate: a fresh plan of the building (ADR-0013 §5, §12; ADR-0010 §2 to §8, §11; I3 step 3,
// I4 step 1): the rooms of the catalog's systems on their floors, each generated by I3's room-level rules; a system
// with fewer distinct titles than world.json's sharedRoomMinTitles takes a section of its floor's shared room, an
// arcade system a section of the arcade room (I4 step 4). The rooms' selections are the catalog's, as the app makes
// them (I3 step 2): SqliteCatalogQuery::roomEntries on a read-only connection, esde::checkRoomMedia against the media
// root of the library <user data>/config/library.json records, then world::selectRoom; nothing is generated while the
// media are unknown (exit 1, ADR-0010 §3). Without --system the building is every system of the catalog that gets a
// room (classify(): not excluded) and has a placeable title, those whose data the asset root cannot give yet left out
// with a note; --system (repeatable) restricts it to those systems, only with --plan or when no plan is stored.
// --selection (repeatable) takes canonical selection files instead (tests, selections kept from elsewhere), each naming
// its system (--system, when given with them, names the same systems); with --replace over a stored plan they must hold
// every system of the stored building. Then the world configuration (the preset under <user data>/config/world.json,
// the seed from --seed when given), the world's data under the asset root, the world's overrides (overrides.json: a
// fresh plan that does not honour a pin is refused), and world::generateBuilding, whose plan is validated
// (world::validatePlan): a plan that breaks a hard rule is never written (exit 3, its findings on stderr). The plan is
// saved as the world's plan under the world lock (rv/world/world_store.hpp, I3 step 9), never over an existing one
// unless --replace asks for the explicit regeneration of the whole building (the face-out sets chosen again, the
// previous plan kept in backups/ first); or written to the file --plan names. Its summary goes to stdout or --output.

